#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "EBi6ka"
msgid "Get help with Deni Run: contact support, connect and disconnect Slack, Notion, and Linear, approvals, and deleting your data."
msgstr "Get help with Deni Run: contact support, connect and disconnect Slack, Notion, and Linear, approvals, and deleting your data."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "WnQ_AZ"
msgid "Contact us"
msgstr "Contact us"

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "Wod8tB"
msgid "Email <mail>{email}</mail> with what you were trying to do, what happened instead, and the email address of your Deni Run account. Screenshots help. We aim to reply within two business days."
msgstr "Email <mail>{email}</mail> with what you were trying to do, what happened instead, and the email address of your Deni Run account. Screenshots help. We aim to reply within two business days."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "FWyUn6"
msgid "Contact the operator of this deployment for help."
msgstr "Contact the operator of this deployment for help."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "M6KKNW"
msgid "Never send passwords, sign-in codes, or access tokens. We will never ask for them."
msgstr "Never send passwords, sign-in codes, or access tokens. We will never ask for them."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "7Rm1x6"
msgid "Frequently asked questions"
msgstr "Frequently asked questions"

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "YdA9eB"
msgid "How do I connect Slack, Notion, Linear, or another app?"
msgstr "How do I connect Slack, Notion, Linear, or another app?"

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "lArnJ6"
msgid "In your workspace, open Plugins, click Browse connectors, search for the app, and click Connect. You sign in on the app’s own site and choose what to allow; Deni Run never sees your password. When you come back, the connector shows Connected and any teammate can use it."
msgstr "In your workspace, open Plugins, click Browse connectors, search for the app, and click Connect. You sign in on the app’s own site and choose what to allow; Deni Run never sees your password. When you come back, the connector shows Connected and any teammate can use it."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "Q6W4lt"
msgid "You can also start from the app’s page under <link>Integrations</link>, for example the “Add to Slack” button. If you are not signed in yet, you sign in first and the connection starts right after."
msgstr "You can also start from the app’s page under <link>Integrations</link>, for example the “Add to Slack” button. If you are not signed in yet, you sign in first and the connection starts right after."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "kpBVbl"
msgid "What needs my approval, and what does “Always allow” do?"
msgstr "What needs my approval, and what does “Always allow” do?"

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "-Zo3B1"
msgid "Tools that a connector marks as read-only, such as searching and reading, run without asking. Every other call, such as posting a message or editing a page, pauses the task and shows an approval card with the tool and what it will send. Nothing is sent until you approve, and if you deny, that step does not run."
msgstr "Tools that a connector marks as read-only, such as searching and reading, run without asking. Every other call, such as posting a message or editing a page, pauses the task and shows an approval card with the tool and what it will send. Nothing is sent until you approve, and if you deny, that step does not run."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "ZUq3Jr"
msgid "“Always allow” is set per connection and per tool in Plugins. When it is on for a tool, a teammate can use that tool without asking you each time. Turn it off in the same menu at any time. For custom MCP servers every tool asks first, even ones the server calls read-only, unless you always allow it."
msgstr "“Always allow” is set per connection and per tool in Plugins. When it is on for a tool, a teammate can use that tool without asking you each time. Turn it off in the same menu at any time. For custom MCP servers every tool asks first, even ones the server calls read-only, unless you always allow it."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "clxGtd"
msgid "Background runs that no one is watching cannot wait for an answer, so there only read-only connector tools run and everything else is declined."
msgstr "Background runs that no one is watching cannot wait for an answer, so there only read-only connector tools run and everything else is declined."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "I1nYNZ"
msgid "How do I disconnect an app?"
msgstr "How do I disconnect an app?"

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "TdhB_w"
msgid "Open Plugins in your workspace and click Disconnect on the app. Teammates lose access right away and Deni Run deletes the sign-in tokens it stored for that app."
msgstr "Open Plugins in your workspace and click Disconnect on the app. Teammates lose access right away and Deni Run deletes the sign-in tokens it stored for that app."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "A0IF2A"
msgid "To remove access on the app’s side as well:"
msgstr "To remove access on the app’s side as well:"

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "VQ0wQj"
msgid "Slack: in Slack, open Tools & settings → Manage apps and remove Deni Run, or ask a workspace admin to remove it."
msgstr "Slack: in Slack, open Tools & settings → Manage apps and remove Deni Run, or ask a workspace admin to remove it."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "52zoAr"
msgid "Notion: disconnect Deni Run from the connections in your Notion settings."
msgstr "Notion: disconnect Deni Run from the connections in your Notion settings."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "1-NFtn"
msgid "Linear: revoke Deni Run from the authorized applications in your Linear account settings."
msgstr "Linear: revoke Deni Run from the authorized applications in your Linear account settings."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "pQmPnH"
msgid "Other connectors: remove Deni Run from the connected or authorized apps in that service’s settings."
msgstr "Other connectors: remove Deni Run from the connected or authorized apps in that service’s settings."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "K3ff74"
msgid "Gmail and Google Drive: remove Deni Run under third-party connections in your Google Account security settings."
msgstr "Gmail and Google Drive: remove Deni Run under third-party connections in your Google Account security settings."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "uw47_9"
msgid "GitHub: revoke Deni Run under Settings → Applications → Authorized OAuth Apps."
msgstr "GitHub: revoke Deni Run under Settings → Applications → Authorized OAuth Apps."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "-UDH4v"
msgid "Discord: click Unlink in Plugins, or send /unlink to the bot."
msgstr "Discord: click Unlink in Plugins, or send /unlink to the bot."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "R-S52x"
msgid "A connector says “Needs sign-in again”. What do I do?"
msgstr "A connector says “Needs sign-in again”. What do I do?"

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "yPElaC"
msgid "The app no longer accepts the saved sign-in. This happens when access was removed on the app’s side, the sign-in expired and could not be renewed, or a workspace admin changed what apps may do. Open Plugins and click Reconnect on that connector to sign in again; your Always allow choices stay as they were."
msgstr "The app no longer accepts the saved sign-in. This happens when access was removed on the app’s side, the sign-in expired and could not be renewed, or a workspace admin changed what apps may do. Open Plugins and click Reconnect on that connector to sign in again; your Always allow choices stay as they were."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "8nQdqr"
msgid "If it keeps asking, disconnect the connector, connect it again, and check that your account on that app can still see what the task needs."
msgstr "If it keeps asking, disconnect the connector, connect it again, and check that your account on that app can still see what the task needs."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "F4WB02"
msgid "Which Slack workspaces does Deni Run work in?"
msgstr "Which Slack workspaces does Deni Run work in?"

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "WnRtJg"
msgid "Any Slack workspace you belong to that allows the app. During sign-in Slack shows which workspace you are connecting; to use a different one, switch workspaces on that screen. Teammates act as you, so they only see the channels, messages, and people your Slack account can see, and messages they post appear as sent by you."
msgstr "Any Slack workspace you belong to that allows the app. During sign-in Slack shows which workspace you are connecting; to use a different one, switch workspaces on that screen. Teammates act as you, so they only see the channels, messages, and people your Slack account can see, and messages they post appear as sent by you."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "0j6T0-"
msgid "If your workspace only allows approved apps, Slack asks you to request approval and a workspace admin must approve Deni Run before you can finish connecting. One Slack connection is kept per Deni Run account; connecting again replaces it."
msgstr "If your workspace only allows approved apps, Slack asks you to request approval and a workspace admin must approve Deni Run before you can finish connecting. One Slack connection is kept per Deni Run account; connecting again replaces it."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "rwGNiN"
msgid "Connecting fails with “This connector is not set up on this server yet”."
msgstr "Connecting fails with “This connector is not set up on this server yet”."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "o55ctT"
msgid "That connector needs app credentials that this deployment has not configured. On run.deniai.app this should not happen, so contact us and we will fix it. If you run your own copy of Deni Run, register an app with the provider (for Slack, set SLACK_MCP_CLIENT_ID and SLACK_MCP_CLIENT_SECRET) and restart the server."
msgstr "That connector needs app credentials that this deployment has not configured. On run.deniai.app this should not happen, so contact us and we will fix it. If you run your own copy of Deni Run, register an app with the provider (for Slack, set SLACK_MCP_CLIENT_ID and SLACK_MCP_CLIENT_SECRET) and restart the server."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "MlJqam"
msgid "Other connection errors are usually cancelled sign-ins or an expired sign-in link. Click Connect again from Plugins and finish the sign-in within a few minutes."
msgstr "Other connection errors are usually cancelled sign-ins or an expired sign-in link. Click Connect again from Plugins and finish the sign-in within a few minutes."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "B552G1"
msgid "How do I delete my data or my account?"
msgstr "How do I delete my data or my account?"

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "jzU68t"
msgid "Disconnecting an app deletes the tokens for it. To export or delete everything, go to <account>Account</account>: deleting your account cancels any subscription and removes your conversations, teammates, connections, workspace files, and computer state. Messages a teammate already posted in Slack or other apps stay there until you delete them in that app. See the <privacy>Privacy Policy</privacy> for what we keep and why."
msgstr "Disconnecting an app deletes the tokens for it. To export or delete everything, go to <account>Account</account>: deleting your account cancels any subscription and removes your conversations, teammates, connections, workspace files, and computer state. Messages a teammate already posted in Slack or other apps stay there until you delete them in that app. See the <privacy>Privacy Policy</privacy> for what we keep and why."

#: app/routes/support.tsx
msgctxt "quvKMJ"
msgid "Can’t sign in? Email <mail>{email}</mail> from the address on your account to request deletion."
msgstr "Can’t sign in? Email <mail>{email}</mail> from the address on your account to request deletion."

#: app/routes/terms.tsx
msgctxt "iSjB38"
msgid "Deni Run is an AI teammate service that can operate a private computer (browser, files, and terminal) on your behalf. By creating an account you agree to these terms."
msgstr "Deni Run is an AI teammate service that can operate a private computer (browser, files, and terminal) on your behalf. By creating an account you agree to these terms."

#: app/routes/terms.tsx
msgctxt "j9MGr2"
msgid "You are responsible for the tasks you assign, including browsing, file changes, and shell commands. Do not use Deni Run to break the law, attack systems, send spam, or process data you are not allowed to handle. Destructive actions may require your approval, but you remain responsible for the outcome."
msgstr "You are responsible for the tasks you assign, including browsing, file changes, and shell commands. Do not use Deni Run to break the law, attack systems, send spam, or process data you are not allowed to handle. Destructive actions may require your approval, but you remain responsible for the outcome."

#: app/routes/terms.tsx
msgctxt "8BzMay"
msgid "You must not use Deni Run to create, edit, or distribute sexual or intimate imagery of a real person without their consent, including AI-generated imagery, or any sexual content involving minors. We remove such content and suspend and report the accounts involved."
msgstr "You must not use Deni Run to create, edit, or distribute sexual or intimate imagery of a real person without their consent, including AI-generated imagery, or any sexual content involving minors. We remove such content and suspend and report the accounts involved."

#: app/routes/terms.tsx
msgctxt "6E7da4"
msgid "Usage limits follow the plan of your linked Deni AI account. Plans, payments, and cancellation are handled by Deni AI under its terms. We may suspend accounts that abuse infrastructure, exceed fair use, or violate these terms."
msgstr "Usage limits follow the plan of your linked Deni AI account. Plans, payments, and cancellation are handled by Deni AI under its terms. We may suspend accounts that abuse infrastructure, exceed fair use, or violate these terms."

#: app/routes/terms.tsx
msgctxt "BARVqC"
msgid "Computer sessions, files, and memory stay scoped to your account. You can export or delete that data from <link>Account</link>. Deleting your account also removes the login stored for this service."
msgstr "Computer sessions, files, and memory stay scoped to your account. You can export or delete that data from <link>Account</link>. Deleting your account also removes the login stored for this service."

#: app/routes/terms.tsx
msgctxt "bXXNWc"
msgid "If you link a Discord account, you are responsible for who can use that account. Anyone who can send direct messages from it can use your workspace much as you can in the app, except account and billing settings: give your teammates tasks, approve actions with the Approve button, change teammates, groups, skills, routines, and plugins, and read or delete workspace files. Discord’s own terms and privacy policy apply to your use of Discord. You can unlink at any time from Plugins or with /unlink."
msgstr "If you link a Discord account, you are responsible for who can use that account. Anyone who can send direct messages from it can use your workspace much as you can in the app, except account and billing settings: give your teammates tasks, approve actions with the Approve button, change teammates, groups, skills, routines, and plugins, and read or delete workspace files. Discord’s own terms and privacy policy apply to your use of Discord. You can unlink at any time from Plugins or with /unlink."

#: app/routes/terms.tsx
msgctxt "PR34Xj"
msgid "Our <link>Privacy Policy</link> explains how we handle your data, including information received from Google sign-in."
msgstr "Our <link>Privacy Policy</link> explains how we handle your data, including information received from Google sign-in."

#: app/routes/terms.tsx
msgctxt "fyPFTO"
msgid "The service is provided as-is. We do not warrant uninterrupted availability. These terms may be updated as the product changes."
msgstr "The service is provided as-is. We do not warrant uninterrupted availability. These terms may be updated as the product changes."

